-- Row il-48. EXPECTED RED: four assertions, all failing, two about each of the two defects. The count (4) is declared in check.sh and in encoding.json.
-- Each states what the citing words need.
-- Defect 1: regulation 7 of the Youth and Apprentices regulations cites section 3(ג) of the Law. The official text says the subsection was repealed
-- (Sefer HaChukim 1621 p. 128, section 2(2), in force from 1 April 1997, section 12 on p. 129), so both fail. Limb (a) is read from the page image.
-- Defect 2: the definition of "השכר הממוצע" cites the 1968 consolidated version of the National Insurance Law. The 1995 consolidated version replaced it from 1 October 1995, so both fail on the LITERAL reading
-- of the citing words. That limb (a) rests on the consolidation's opening notice of the 1995 version is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY, and the reading through the Interpretation Law section 25, under which the first
-- assertion would pass, is recorded as a green test in il48-tests-xrefs.l4 and as fork P2 in NOTES.md. Nothing here is edited to make it pass.

§ `Defect 1: the citing words need a subsection that is not there`

-- 1. The description of the target is not the description of what the citing words point at.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`)
-- 2. The text the citing words name is not in force on a day long after the repeal.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: youth regulation 7 to s 3(ג), the premium rule`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Defect 2: the citing words name a version that was replaced`

-- 3. The description of the target is not the description of what the citing words point at (the literal reading).
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`)
-- 4. The version the citing words name is not in force on a day long after its replacement.
#ASSERT `the named text is in force on` (`reference: definition of the average wage to NII 1968 s 1`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
